<div id="device_preferences">
	<h1><tmpl_var _("webui", "preferences_device_preference_sub_header_text")></h1>
	<p>
		This screen contains many options which allow you to set the behaviour of the <tmpl_var _("webui", "webui_product_name")> to better meet your needs.
	</p>

	<tmpl_if usbmodeShow>
		<h3><tmpl_var truncate(_("webui", "preferences_usb_mode_label"), (size(_("webui", "preferences_usb_mode_label")) - size(":")))></h3>
		<p>
			This settings determines the connection type when a computer is connected to the <tmpl_var _("webui", "webui_product_name_with_suffix")> USB C port. Select the desired option.
		</p>
	</tmpl_if>

	<tmpl_if usbPromptShow>
		<h3><tmpl_var truncate(_("webui", "preferences_usb_connection_prompt_label"), (size(_("webui", "preferences_usb_connection_prompt_label")) - size(":")))></h3>
		<p>
			If checked, then you will be prompted (on the <tmpl_var _("webui", "webui_product_name")>'s screen) to select the desired USB mode when a USB connection to a computer is detected. Making a selection on this prompt does not change the setting above, but only sets the mode for the current USB session.
		</p>
	</tmpl_if>
	
	<h3>
		<tmpl_var truncate(_("webui", "preferences_turnoff_diplay_label"), (size(_("webui", "preferences_turnoff_diplay_label")) - size(":")))>
	</h3>
	<p>
		This setting determines how quickly the <tmpl_var _("webui", "webui_product_name_with_suffix")> screen will turn off, after a period of inactivity. Select the desired option.
	</p>

	<tmpl_if deepSleepModeShow>
		<h3>
			<tmpl_var truncate(_("webui", "preferences_deep_sleep_label"), (size(_("webui", "preferences_deep_sleep_label")) - size(":")))>
		</h3>
		<p>
			The <tmpl_var _("webui", "webui_product_name")> will enter sleep mode after a period of inactivity. Select the desired time period to enter sleep mode.
		</p>
	</tmpl_if>

	<tmpl_if autoShutdownShow>
		<h3>
			<tmpl_var truncate(_("webui", "preferences_auto_shutdown_label"), (size(_("webui", "preferences_auto_shutdown_label")) - size(":")))>
		</h3>
		<p>
			The <tmpl_var _("webui", "webui_product_name")> can shutdown after a period of inactivity. Select the desired time period to trigger a shutdown.
		</p>
	</tmpl_if>	
	
	<tmpl_if universalChargingShow>
		<h2>
			<tmpl_var _("webui", "preferences_universal_charging_sub_header_text")>
		</h2>
		<p>
			This feature allows you to charge devices such as your phone or Bluetooth headset from the <tmpl_var _("webui", "webui_product_name_with_suffix")> battery. Simply connect your device's USB cable to the <tmpl_var _("webui", "webui_product_name_with_suffix")> Universal Charging port.
		</p>
	
		<h3>
			<tmpl_var truncate(_("webui", "preferences_universal_charging_status_label"), (size(_("webui", "preferences_universal_charging_status_label")) - size(":")))>
		</h3>
		<p>
			This field displays the current status of the Universal Charging feature. Possible status values are:
		</p>

		<blockquote>
			<ul>
				<li>
			   		<tmpl_var _("preferences_universal_charging_status_charging_text")> - an external devices is being charged from the <tmpl_var _("webui", "webui_product_name_with_suffix")> battery.
			   	</li>
			   	<li>
			   		<tmpl_var _("preferences_universal_charging_status_available_text")> - if an external device is connected to the <tmpl_var _("webui", "webui_product_name_with_suffix")> Universal Charging Port, it will be charged.
			   	</li>
			   	<li>
			   		<tmpl_var _("preferences_universal_charging_status_not_available_text")> - the <tmpl_var _("webui", "webui_product_name_with_suffix")> battery is too low to charge other devices. 
			   	</li>
				</ul>
		</blockquote>
	</tmpl_if>

	<tmpl_if displaySettingsShow>
		<h2><tmpl_udf  GET_PO_TEXT("preferences_display_settings_toggle_label", gProductName)></h2>
		<p>
			If ON, then the available settings can be changed using the <tmpl_var _("webui", "webui_product_name_with_suffix")> screen. These settings include a factory reset operation, which resets all settings to the factory default values.
		</p>
		<p>
			If OFF, then changing settings using the <tmpl_var _("webui", "webui_product_name_with_suffix")> screen is not possible. 
		</p>
	</tmpl_if>
	
	<h2><tmpl_udf  GET_PO_TEXT("preferences_hardware_reset_toggle_label", gProductName)></h2>	
	<p>
		If ON, the reset button on the base of the <tmpl_var _("webui", "webui_product_name")> functions normally, changing all settings to the factory default values.
	</p>
	<p>
		If OFF, the reset button does not function. This prevents a user from changing settings by performing a reset.
	</p>	

	<tmpl_if EthernetEnableShow>
		<h2><tmpl_udf  GET_PO_TEXT("preferences_enable_ethernet_port_toggle_label", gProductName)></h2>
		<p>
			To use ethernet, please enable the ethernet port via the Settings menu.<br><br>Note: When enabled, the ethernet port will increase battery consumption. It is recommended you keep your device plugged into the AC charger during ethernet use. To reduce battery consumption, disable ethernet when not in use.
		</p>
	</tmpl_if>
	<tmpl_if batteryPreservationModeShow>
	<h2><tmpl_udf  GET_PO_TEXT("preferences_battery_preservation_mode_toggle_label", gProductName)></h2>	
	<p>
		Battery Preservation Mode extends your battery life by maintaining a battery level between <tmpl_var batteryHealthMinThreshold>% and <tmpl_var batteryHealthMaxThreshold>%. This mode is recommended if you frequently charge your device for extended periods of time. When enabled, Battery Preservation Mode will be activated after an extended period of continuous charge.
	</p>
	</tmpl_if>
</div>
